---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What exactly does Crontinel monitor?',
    a: `Crontinel watches background jobs in whatever runtime already runs them. Every job can send an HTTP receipt with the exit code and a business result such as <code class="text-green-400 bg-gray-800 px-1 rounded text-xs">processed_records</code>. Exit 0 can still fail when the work produced nothing. The Laravel package is the deep integration for schedule attach, queue depth, and Horizon freshness.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How is this different from Healthchecks.io or Cronitor?',
    a: `Healthchecks.io is a strong dead man's switch. Cronitor covers broad job monitoring and custom metrics. Crontinel focuses on outcome rules: a completed process and a failed business result stay separate, missing evidence is never shown as healthy, and your coding assistant can read a cited evidence packet over MCP. Laravel depth (schedule, queues, Horizon) is optional on top of the same receipt.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it work with frameworks other than Laravel?',
    a: `Yes. Five common runtimes are first-class: curl (system cron), Node, Python, Sidekiq/Ruby, and GitHub Actions. Each posts the same HTTP receipt. See the <a href="https://docs.crontinel.com/check-in/recipes/" class="text-green-400 underline">check-in recipes</a>. Unowned language SDKs are not a support claim. Laravel remains the maintained deep package for schedule, queue, and Horizon.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a free tier?',
    a: `Starter, Pro, and Max are the planned paid tiers. Public price-card details stay unpublished until billing acceptance. Sign up at app.crontinel.com to evaluate with a real job receipt.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I get started?',
    a: `Create an app, copy the ingest key (not an MCP key), and POST a receipt to <code class="text-green-400 bg-gray-800 px-1 rounded text-xs">/api/v1/ingest/cron</code> when the job finishes. Send <code class="text-green-400 bg-gray-800 px-1 rounded text-xs">processed_records: 0</code>, confirm the outcome alert, then send a later count and confirm recovery. Laravel apps can additionally <code class="text-green-400 bg-gray-800 px-1 rounded text-xs">composer require crontinel/laravel</code> for schedule, queue, and Horizon.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What alert channels are supported?',
    a: `Email failure and recovery alerts are the verified launch path. Slack and customer webhooks are planned for paid tiers after the same failure/recovery checks pass. Do not treat SMS or on-call rotations as part of this offer.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I self-host everything or do I need the SaaS?',
    a: `Hosted detection is the product path for independent alerts when the customer's scheduler dies. A package that only alerts locally on the same host is not a substitute. The Laravel package is open source; outcome evaluation and alerting run on app.crontinel.com.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What does pricing look like for a small team?',
    a: `Planned public prices are Starter $9.99, Pro $19.99, and Max $49.99 monthly, with matching annual totals. Checkout and entitlement acceptance remain open before the public price card is the source of truth.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the MCP server for?',
    a: `Hosted MCP (OAuth first, scoped API key second) lets Cursor, Claude Code, or Codex read incidents and evidence. Ordinary reads do not spend the hosted AI allowance. The assistant must not declare the job healthy; a later passing receipt clears the incident.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is this package open source?',
    a: `The Laravel package (<code class="text-green-400 bg-gray-800 px-1 rounded text-xs">crontinel/laravel</code>) is MIT-licensed. The hosted app at app.crontinel.com is the commercial product. Other language repos may exist on GitHub without being a supported install path for outcome receipts.`,
  },
];---

<Base
  title="Crontinel FAQ: Pricing, Self-Hosting & Monitoring"
  description="Common questions about Crontinel: what it monitors, how it compares to alternatives, pricing, self-hosting, and getting started."
>
<script type="application/ld+json" slot="head">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://crontinel.com" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "FAQ", "item": "https://crontinel.com/faq/" }
  ]
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json" slot="head">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What exactly does Crontinel monitor?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Crontinel watches background jobs in any runtime via an HTTP outcome receipt. Exit 0 can still fail when the business result is empty. The Laravel package adds schedule, queue, and Horizon evidence."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is this different from Healthchecks.io or Cronitor?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Healthchecks.io is a dead man's switch. Cronitor covers broad job monitoring. Crontinel separates process completion from business result, never treats missing evidence as healthy, and gives coding assistants a cited MCP evidence packet."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does it work with frameworks other than Laravel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Five common runtimes are first-class: curl, Node, Python, Sidekiq/Ruby, and GitHub Actions. See docs.crontinel.com/check-in/recipes/. Laravel is the maintained deep package. Unowned language SDKs are not a support claim."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is there a free tier?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Starter, Pro, and Max are the planned paid tiers. Public price-card details stay unpublished until billing acceptance. Sign up at app.crontinel.com to evaluate with a real job receipt."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I get started?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Create an app, copy the ingest key, and POST a receipt to /api/v1/ingest/cron when the job finishes. Verify a zero count and a recovery. Laravel apps can use composer require crontinel/laravel for schedule, queue, and Horizon."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What alert channels are supported?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Email failure and recovery alerts are the verified launch path. Slack and customer webhooks are planned for paid tiers after the same checks pass."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I self-host everything or do I need the SaaS?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Hosted detection is the product path for independent alerts. A local-only package is not a substitute when the same host dies. The Laravel package is open source; outcome evaluation runs on app.crontinel.com."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does pricing look like for a small team?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Planned public prices are Starter $9.99, Pro $19.99, and Max $49.99 monthly. Checkout acceptance remains open before the public price card is final."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the MCP server for?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Hosted MCP (OAuth first, scoped API key second) lets Cursor, Claude Code, or Codex read incidents and evidence. Ordinary reads do not spend the hosted AI allowance. The assistant must not declare the job healthy."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is this package open source?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Laravel package is MIT-licensed. The hosted app at app.crontinel.com is the commercial product. Other language repos may exist without being a supported outcome-receipt install path."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>

  <Nav />

  <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16" id="main-content">
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">FAQ</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400">
        Common questions about installation, plans, data privacy, and how Crontinel works.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <div class="border-b border-gray-800 pb-10">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">{item.q}</h2>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed" set:html={item.a} />
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 border border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 text-center">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Something not covered here?</p>
      <a
        href="https://discord.com/invite/clawd"
        class="inline-block text-sm text-green-400 hover:text-green-300 transition-colors"
      >
        Ask in the Discord community &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
